WEBVTT

00:31:58.100 --> 00:32:00.847
How do you break through
that pressure and get heard

00:32:00.871 --> 00:32:02.536
when people don't want to listen?

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:04.037
CM: When you're a minority,

00:32:04.061 --> 00:32:08.556
however you might be a minority
in an organization,

00:32:08.580 --> 00:32:11.496
you're already a rebel.

00:32:11.520 --> 00:32:14.136
AG: To get her career
back on track at the CIA,

00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:16.571
Carmen Medina didn't have to
suppress her identity

00:32:16.595 --> 00:32:18.346
as an original thinker.

00:32:18.370 --> 00:32:20.476
But she did need to
build up her reputation

00:32:20.500 --> 00:32:22.557
as someone committed to the mission.

00:32:23.430 --> 00:32:26.246
And so this is guideline number three:

00:32:26.270 --> 00:32:28.655
authenticity without status and trust

00:32:28.679 --> 00:32:29.837
is risky.